-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",63,{
[1985]="7000E069\n1\tFind Narchuil\tThe Elf-captain or his belongings may remain within the cave. Saija suggested you speak with her again to seek out the cave, and she would guide you there. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Arvedui\tThe shade of Arvedui is at the Ruin of Thoroval north and east along the Ice Bay in Talvi-mûri. Having recovered a ring-fragment from Aearil's belongings, you should seek out the shade of Arvedui and let him know the fate of his would-be rescuer and learn whether the fragment you found is indeed the lost half of Narchuil.\n",
[1986]="7001016A\n1\tTalk to Eglamír at Celondim\tEglamír is at Celondim in Ered Luin, far to the west of Bree-land. Newbold Leafcutter suggested you return to Eglamír for more advice.\n",
[1987]="7001016B\n1\tTalk to Yrjänä at Sûri-kylä\tYrjänä is at Sûri-kylä in Forochel, far to the east and north of Celondim. Eglamír believes that Amarthiel's minions may be trying to find the lair of a dragon which may still dwell in Forochel, the hide from which may be used to repair the bellows of the forges at Mirobel. He suggests you go to the frozen north and speak with the Lossoth chieftain Yrjänä.\n",
[1988]="7001016C\n1\tFind and enter Bregmor's lair\tBregmor's lair can be found far to the west of Sûri-kylä, south-east of Jotunstath. Yrjänä told you that the dragon Bregmor once terrorized Forochel, but no longer. He also indicated that he would not spare his people to guide you to Bregmor's lair, leaving you to fend for yourself. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Yrjänä at Sûri-kylä\tYrjänä is at Sûri-kylä, far to the east of Bregmor's lair. You failed to stop Angmar from obtaining the hide of the dragon Bregmor and should now return to Yrjänä with your news.\n",
[1989]="7001016D\n1\tTalk to Eglamír at Celondim\tEglamír is at Celondim in Ered Luin, far to the south and west of Forochel. Yrjänä told you to return to Eglamír with news of your failure.\n",
[1990]="7001016E\n1\tTalk to Elrond at Rivendell\tElrond is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws, far to the east of Celondim. Eglamír suggested that you bring news of your failure to Elrond at Rivendell.\n",
[1991]="7001016F\n1\tTravel to Mirobel and try to stop Amarthiel\tMirobel can be reached by travelling far to the south, into the land of Eregion. Elrond instructed you to journey to Mirobel and do whatever you can to stop Amarthiel. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to the watch-captain\tThe watch-captain Glorenthol is at Delossad in Tâl Bruinen. You failed to stop Amarthiel, but she was at last defeated at the surprise return of Mordirith. Narchuil has fallen into the hands of the False King, but Amarthiel is now the prisoner of the Free Peoples. You should speak with the watch-captain Glorenthol.\n3\tTalk to Elrond at Rivendell\tElrond is in his library at the Last Homely House in Rivendell. The watch-captain has directed you to speak with Elrond regarding your mission to Mirobel.\n",
[1992]="70010170\n1\tBring the fine clover honey to Filegnaneth\030Find fine clover honey (total: 5)\tThe expert cook is in Michel Delving in the Shire, far to the west of Rivendell. Filegnaneth is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws, far to the east of the Shire. Filegnaneth has asked you to travel to the Shire and purchase fine clover honey from the expert cook there.\n",
[1993]="7003E287\n1\tTalk to Théoden on the field of victory at Helm's Deep, after sunrise\tThéoden King is to the south of Gandalf, on the field before the Hornburg, after sunrise. Gandalf has given you a number of healing poultices and wants you to tend to the hurts of the King and his men.\n2\tIssue Théoden's command to men who own swift horses (total: 3)\030Treat injured men with healing poultices (total: 3)\tGandalf has asked you to bring healing poultices to injured men in Helm's Deep, and the King has asked you to bring his command to any men nearby who own swift horses.\n3\tTalk to Erkenbrand on the field of victory outside the Hornburg, after sunrise\tErkenbrand is on the field of battle outside the Hornburg, after sunrise. Théoden asked you to find Erkenbrand on the field of victory and to thank him for his timely arrival.\n4\tTalk to Erkenbrand on the field of victory outside the Hornburg, after sunrise\tErkenbrand is on the field of battle outside the Hornburg, after sunrise. Théoden asked you to find Erkenbrand on the field of victory and to thank him for his timely arrival.\n5\tTalk to Éomer on the field of victory outside the Hornburg, after sunrise\tÉomer is on the field of victory outside the Hornburg, after sunrise.\n6\tTalk to Déorwine inside the fortress of the Hornburg, after sunrise\tDéorwine is inside the fortress of the Hornburg, after sunrise. Éomer thinks you should rest for a few hours inside the fortress of the Hornburg, before going with the King's company to the Ring of Isengard to confront Saruman.\n",
[1994]="70010172\n1\tBring Laerdan's breastplate back to Golodir at Gath Forthnír\030Find Laerdan's breastplate\tDolendath is located in Imlad Balchorth, south and west of Myrkworth. Golodir suggested that you may find Laerdan's breastplate at Dolendath, the place where Golodir's army first took refuge in Angmar. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n",
[1995]="70010169\n1\tTalk to Filegnaneth in Rivendell\030Talk to Nat Collop at Tinnudír\030Talk to Golodir at Gath Forthnír\tFilegnaneth is found in the Hall of Fire at Rivendell. Nat Collop is found in Tinnudír in Evendim, far to the west and north of the Trollshaws. Golodir is found in Gath Forthnír in Angmar, far to the north of the Trollshaws. Laerdan asked you to perform several tasks on his behalf.\n2\tExamine Laerdan's Note\tLaerdan is at the Last Homely House in Rivendell. You should return at once to Laerdan with news of your successes, but also of the resulting delays.\n3\tTalk to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is in his library in the Last Homely House at Rivendell. You should tell Elrond of Laerdan's note at once.\n",
[1996]="70010171\n1\tBring the dwarf-steel cutlery moulds to Nat Collop at Tinnudír\030Find dwarf-steel cutlery moulds (total: 5)\tThorin's Hall is in Ered Luin, far to the west and south of Evendim. Nat Collop has asked you to speak with the expert metalsmith at Thorin's Hall and obtain some dwarf-steel cutlery moulds.\n",
[1997]="7003E292\n1\tTalk to Déorwine and rest before setting out with the company\tDéorwine is inside the keep of the Hornburg, after sunrise, at Helm's Deep. Déorwine is waiting for your word, and then he will prepare a place for you to rest before setting out for Isengard with the King.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad is on the road beyond the Fords of Isen. You have both been through much, and Halbarad greatly wishes to hear what has transpired since last you spoke.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn is beyond the Fords of Isen, and wishes to speak with you.\n",
[1998]="70010173\n1\tTalk to Ladrochan at the stable in Rivendell\tLadrochan, the stable-master, can be found in the stables of Rivendell, west of the Last Homely House. Elrond has told you to speak with Ladrochan and learn how long ago Laerdan left Rivendell.\n2\tTalk to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is in his library in the Last Homely House of Rivendell, to the east of the stable. Ladrochan told you that Laerdan had left Rivendell two days ago. You should return to Elrond with this news at once.\n",
[1999]="70010174\n1\tExamine Coil of Rope\030Examine Pack\030Examine Map of Eregion\tLaerdan's room is in the Last Homely House in Rivendell. Elrond has asked you to search Laerdan's rooms for anything which might reveal Laerdan's full purpose.\n2\tExamine Laerdan's journal\tElrond is in the library at the Last Homely House in Rivendell. You found a journal in Laerdan's rooms. It may reveal Laerdan's plans.\n",
[2000]="7003E293\n1\tRide along the road north to Isengard, and remain alert\tAragorn has asked you to ride along the road to Isengard, and to keep your eyes peeled as you go.\n2\tTalk to Gandalf by the Pillar of the Hand\tGandalf stands by the Pillar of the Hand, on the way to Isengard.\n3\tRide north to the gate of Isengard\tGandalf has warned you that you might not recognize Isengard since last you saw it.\n4\tTalk to Pippin\tYou have found Merry and Pippin at the gate of Isengard.\n",
[2001]="70010175\n1\tRead Laerdan's journal further and experience 'Session: The Prisoner of Sammath Baul' or read the shortened account instead\tYou should read further into the journal... it may provide some clues as to Laerdan's purposes. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tFinish reading the journal\tWhile reading Laerdan's journal, you discover that Laerdan believes he saw his daughter Narmeleth there at Sammath Baul. This entry is quite disturbing....\n",
[2002]="7003E294\n1\tTalk to Merry\tMerry is outside the gate of Isengard.\n2\tEnter the gate-house and look for the pipe-weed Merry mentioned\tMerry asked you to go inside the gate-house and bring out some more of the pipe-weed they found there.\n3\tEnter the gate-house and look for the pipe-weed Merry mentioned\tMerry asked you to go inside the gate-house and bring out some more of the pipe-weed they found there.\n4\tBring the pipe-weed to Merry outside the gate-house\tMerry asked you to go inside the gate-house and bring out some more of the pipe-weed they found there.\n5\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn is outside the gate-house at Isengard, and wears a concerned expression.\n",
[2003]="70010176\n1\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond is found in the Library of the Last Homely House in Rivendell. You should return at once to Elrond and tell him what you have learned.\n",
[2004]="7003E297\n1\tTalk to Gandalf by the base of Orthanc\tGandalf is at the base of Orthanc, considering what to do about the Wizard waiting within.\n2\tTalk to Treebeard at the base of Orthanc\tTreebeard is by the base of Orthanc. Gandalf has asked you to speak with Treebeard while he considers what to do about Saruman.\n3\tExplore west of Orthanc\030Explore south of Orthanc\030Explore north of Orthanc\tTreebeard believes you should search within the Ring of Isengard for any sign of your captive friend.\n4\tTalk to Gandalf at the base of Orthanc\tGandalf is at the base of Orthanc, waiting to hear what you discovered in your search of the flooded Ring.\n",
[2005]="7003E2A5\n1\tFind the entrance to the Isengard Depths, north of Orthanc\tAn entrance to the Isengard Depths can be found north of the tower. Gandalf believes Lothrandir may still live, and wants you to search for news of him in the caverns below Isengard.\n2\tTalk to Golodir in the Isengard Depths\tGolodir also searches the Isengard Depths for news of Lothrandir.\n3\tDefeat surly scavenger ([see journal]/6)\tSurly scavengers can be found throughout the Isengard Depths. Golodir has asked you to defeat the scavengers that lurk within the flooded depths of Isengard, for one of them might know of Lothrandir's location, if the Ranger still lives.\n4\tDefeat surly scavenger (5/6)\tSurly scavengers can be found throughout the Isengard Depths. Golodir has asked you to defeat the scavengers that lurk within the flooded depths of Isengard, for one of them might know of Lothrandir's location, if the Ranger still lives.\n5\tTalk to Golodir\tGolodir is in the flooded depths beneath Isengard, waiting to hear the results of your search.\n",
[2006]="70010177\n1\tDiscuss with Elrond what fate may await Laerdan and experience 'Session: The Fate of Laerdan' or read the shortened account instead\tElrond is in his library at the Last Homely House in Rivendell. Elrond wishes to speak with you regarding what he discovered in Laerdan's journal. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond is in his library at the Last Homely House in Rivendell. You discussed the fate of Laerdan with Elrond, coming to a dire conclusion.\n",
[2007]="7003E2A7\n1\tTalk to Halbarad north-west of Orthanc\tHalbarad is in the Ring of Isengard, north-west of Orthanc, looking for Lothrandir. Golodir has asked you to return to the surface and to help Halbarad with his search for the captive Ranger.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad and continue his search for Lothrandir\tHalbarad is in the Ring of Isengard, north-west of Orthanc, looking for Lothrandir. Halbarad is waiting to go with you to search further buildings in Isengard for Lothrandir.\n3\tTalk to Halbarad north-west of Orthanc, within the Ring of Isengard\tHalbarad is north-west of Orthanc.\n",
[2008]="70010178\n1\tSearch for Eglamír in Celondim\tElrond spoke of an Elf named Eglamír who may dwell in Celondim in Ered Luin, far to the west of Rivendell and the Trollshaws. Elrond has told you that Celebrimbor wisely did not record many of the details of Ring-craft in the lore of Eregion. However Elrond did find many references to an Elf named Eglamír who may know more.\n",
[2009]="7003E2A8\n1\tTalk to Aragorn at the base of Orthanc\tAragorn is on the stairs at the base of Orthanc.\n2\tTalk to Gandalf on the steps of Orthanc\030Talk to Théoden on the steps of Orthanc\030Talk to Pippin by the foot of the steps\tGandalf, Théoden, and Pippin all witnessed the confrontation with Saruman and wish to speak with you about the Wizard's schemes.\n3\tTalk to Halbarad by the base of Orthanc\tHalbarad has come to the base of Orthanc.\n",
[2010]="70010179\n1\tTalk to Barliman Butterbur\030Talk to Chief Watcher Grimbriar\030Talk to Mayor Graeme Tenderlarch\tBree-town lies in Bree-land, far to the east of Ered Luin. Eglamír would speak little of the Ring-lore of Eregion, but did tell you that the Ring-smith Celebrimbor gave a shaping tool to a Man of Bree-land. He suggests you find someone in Bree who might know the whereabouts of the Man's barrow.\n2\tTalk to Newbold Leafcutter\tNewbold Leafcutter can be found at the Scholar's Stairs Archive in Bree-town. You were advised to seek out Newbold Leafcutter to learn more regarding the whereabouts of Celebrimbor's shaping tool.\n",
[2011]="7001017A\n1\tFind the tomb of Maenadar the Craftsman\tThe tomb of Maenadar can be found in the small barrow beside the entrance to Haudh Iarchith in the southern parts of the Barrow-downs. Newbold Leafcutter told you that the shaping tool can be found in the tomb of Maenadar the Craftsman.\n2\tTalk to Newbold Leafcutter in Bree\tNewbold Leafcutter is at the Scholar's Stairs Archive in Bree-town. You came too late to the tomb of Maenadar and found it despoiled. Angmar arrived first. You should return to Newbold Leafcutter to learn if he knows anything else.\n",
[2012]="700169E4\n1\tTalk to Narmeleth at Gath Forthnír\tNarmeleth is in her father's old room at Gath Forthnír in the northern reaches of Angmar. Narmeleth has told you to speak with Golodir and find what has become of the broken blade of Dúnachar.\n2\tTalk to Golodir\tGolodir is in his room in Gath Forthnír. Narmeleth has told you to speak with Golodir and find what has become of the broken blade of Dúnachar.\n",
[2013]="700169E5\n1\tRetrieve the broken hilt of Dúnachar\tLorniel's grave is on the northern slopes of Gorothlad, south of Nan Gurth in Angmar. Golodir has given you the location of Dúnachar and has given you permission to retrieve it.\n2\tBring the hilt to Golodir\tGolodir is at Gath Forthnír in the northern reaches of Angmar. You should return to Golodir with the broken hilt of Dúnachar.\n",
[2014]="700169E6\n1\tBring the hilt to Narmeleth\tGath Forthnír is in the northern reaches of Angmar. Golodir told you to bring the hilt to Narmeleth in Gath Forthnír. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tAssault Gador Gúlaran\tNarmeleth is in Gath Forthnír in the northern reaches of Angmar. Narmeleth told you to gather friends and speak with her again to begin the final assault. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n3\tTalk to Golodir at Gath Forthnír\tGath Forthnír is in the northern reaches of Angmar. You should speak with Golodir in Gath Forthnír.\n4\tTalk to Glorfindel in Rivendell\tRivendell is in the north-east corner of the Trollshaws. Golodir sent you to speak with Glorfindel and bring him news of Mordirith's defeat.\n5\tTalk to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond can be found in the Last Homely House in Rivendell. Glorfindel told you to deliver your tidings to Master Elrond.\n6\tTalk to Failloth in Rivendell\tFailloth is in the courtyard of the Last Homely House in Rivendell. Elrond told you to retrieve Laerdan's legacy from Failloth, the caretakers of Rivendell.\n",
[2015]="700169E3\n1\tTalk to Glorfindel in Rivendell\tGlorfindel can be found outside the Last Homely House to the south-east, looking out on the Falls of Imladris. Elrond has asked you to speak with Glorfindel.\n2\tTalk to Narmeleth at Delossad\tDelossad is south-west of Rivendell in Tâl Bruinen, east of Garbert's cottage. Glorfindel has asked that you question Narmeleth in Delossad.\n",
[2016]="700169E7\n1\tTalk to Halbarad at Esteldín\tEsteldín is in the North Downs, a land north-west of the Trollshaws. Narmeleth wishes for you to travel to Esteldín and warn Halbarad of the spy.\n",
})
